# Central Pi

Runs the FastAPI API and the RabbitMQ consumer that persists telemetry.

## Required environment variables

- CENTRAL_PI_API_KEY
- CENTRAL_PI_RABBITMQ_URL

Optional:

- CENTRAL_PI_QUEUE_NAME (default: sensor_data_queue)

## Run locally

1) Install deps:

pip install -r requirements.txt

2) Start API:

CENTRAL_PI_API_KEY=changeme uvicorn central_pi.server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

3) Start consumer (separate shell):

CENTRAL_PI_RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://sensor:sensorpass@<queue-pi-ip>:5672/sensors_vhost \
python -m central_pi.consumer

## systemd (on Pi)

1) Copy project to /opt/central_pi and create /etc/central_pi.env
2) Install services:

sudo cp systemd/central-pi-api.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo cp systemd/central-pi-consumer.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now central-pi-api central-pi-consumer

## Install script

Run from the repo root:

sudo bash central_pi/scripts/install.sh
